--TEST--
hovering a key in an object literal written where a shape type is declared shows the key's field and the `///` doc above it in that shape, `rule:types/shape-type`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Mailer
{
    public static function send(
        {
            /// The address the message goes to.
            to: string,
            /// The line shown before the message is opened.
            subject?: string,
        } $message,
    ): void {}
}

Mailer::send({to: "a@example.com", sub<|>ject: "Hello"});
--REQUEST--
hover
--EXPECT--
```nvs
subject?: string
```

The line shown before the message is opened.
